Corrections, June 2026

This fork fixes 2,135 joined-word errors in the play texts, restoring
2,136 missing spaces. Neighbouring words had been run together. Macbeth
read "the fatalbellman" for "the fatal bellman".
Twelfth Night read "in startsdistractedly" for "in starts distractedly".
The same defect runs through every play file, roughly once per page.

The fixes insert the missing spaces and nothing else. One error was three
words run together and needed two spaces. Spelling, casing, punctuation
and wording stay exactly as the editions print them. Elisions and verse are
unaffected. Names such as Robin Goodfellow and real archaic words such as
"clotpole" were checked and left alone.

Candidate errors were found by scanning for rare joined words that split
cleanly into two real words. Each split was then verified against an
independent edition of the complete works, most at passage level with the
surrounding words matching. Everything the scan could not verify was
reviewed by hand, word by word, across several review rounds.

The full list of changes is in corrections/fixed-words.tsv. One row per
fix: file, line, the joined word, and the corrected text.

The First Folio files are not corrected in this pass.

Corrections by iamiq, June 2026. These changes are released under the same
GFDL 1.3 licence as the texts. The original PlayShakespeare.com copyright
and licence notices above are unchanged.
